flaws:
Too many budget mechanisms to run by hand. The design uses:
- shared.spend_budget per_run/per_day rows;
- a new hard-coded monthly ceiling (cost_guard has no DFS monthly period today, so this is new ledger-sum code);
- an env kill switch QUESTION_FILL_ENABLED;
- a per-run usd_cap;
- a 'standing 3 USD/month approval';
- separate approvals for the 182-day and 365-day refreshes.
Six knobs across DB, code, env and process is a lot for one engineer to keep consistent. Budgets read from the ledger can also be bypassed by the off-ledger spender, and the design does not make the guard reconcile the balance.
